  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "You’d like to convert the cafeteria meal data from [the spreadsheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1bpIy7wASa0nNpZ3P3ia3CQr5iAK_hUAFjT2jb7-rCJ0/edit?usp=sharing) to a CSV file so that Python programs can more easily work with the data.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Populate `meals.csv` with data from at least three rows from the spreadsheet. Remember to also include a header row with column names!\r\n2. Press “Run” to see a visual representation of the CSV file and verify that it looks like what you expect.",
